==Spanish==

===Etymology===
{{unk.|es}}, maybe related to French {{term|lang=fr|gai}}, Italian {{term|lang=it|gaio}}, English {{term|lang=en|gay}} of Germanic origin or from Arabic {{term|lang=ar|كويس||kuwayyis|bueno}}

===Adjective===
{{head|es|adjective}}

# {{Spain|slang|lang=es}} [[cool]]

====Usage notes====
* This adjective is most often treated as invariable, with the form {{term||guay|lang=es}} being used regardless of gender or number; however, the plural form {{term|guays|lang=es}} is also often found. Hence, “They're very cool” may be expressed either as ''son muy guay'' or as ''son muy guays''.

===Adverb===
{{es-adv}}

# {{Spain|slang|lang=es}} [[cool]]

====Usage notes====
* Often expanded to '''guay de Paraguay'''.

